Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:29:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 561/572] plat(stm32mp2): add stm32mp_init_retram

Add a specific function to initialized the RETRAM before to use it to
save the DDR PHY settings; BL2 activate the ECC when it is not yet done
on cold boot, when RAMCFG is not used by ROM code (CLOSED/LOCKED chip).

With this patch the RETRAM configuration (ECC and ALE activated, SRAM
hardware erase disable) for cold boot, when ECC is activated or not by
ROM code, and for standby exit (RAMCFG_RETRAMCR= 0x1011).
Moreover the ECC and SRAM erase bit are protected and remove the
access to RAMCFG_RETRAMCR register in BL31 power management
initialization function.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 90ad5b327591c64d60a202c6325569221963c340 plat(stm32mp2): add stm32mp_init_retram]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I60c92022ebceda92ecbb285a3d92f4260ab85d25
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/605800
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/st/ddr/stm32mp2_ram.c           |  2 +
 plat/st/common/include/stm32mp_common.h |  3 +-
